PART 1 — the fix fires on EVERY HDR crop (loop skipped, blowup eliminated):
  e9 d4: default == --no-butteraugli byte-identical on 88/88 crops
  (LOOP-SKIPPED=88, NOT-SKIPPED=0, FAIL-ENCODE=0). The gate
  (is_hdr_pq_hlg AND resolved hdr_loss==Vdp2) is content-independent, so it
  fires for all PQ/HLG content — no crop slips it. Before the fix these e8/e9
  encodes ran the VDP2 loop and over-refined +100..500 % bytes.

PART 2 — with the loop skipped, our HDR e9 default now BEATS cjxl on bytes
  corpus-wide (matched requested distance):
