            4415878 = -6.1 % vs cjxl
    e9 d4:  ours <= cjxl bytes on 74/88 crops;  total ours 1358434 vs cjxl
            1399753 = -3.0 % vs cjxl
  (Quality: the 6-crop RD sweep hdr_loop_rd_sweep_2026-07-15.tsv established the
  no-loop base sits ON or INSIDE cjxl's RD curve — at d4 it wins BOTH bytes AND
  VDP2 on the checked crops. These matched-distance byte totals are the corpus-
  scale confirmation that the base is competitive-to-better, not just non-blown-up.)

VERDICT: the e8/e9 HDR buttloop over-refinement (the dominant HDR RD gap, missed
